Sure! Here's a simple example of how you can place a **clickable SVG icon (reading glass icon)** to the **right side of an input field**, and have it trigger a function when clicked.

### ✅ HTML + JavaScript Example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Search Input with Icon</title>
  <style>
    .search-container {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-block;
    }

    .search-input {
      padding-right: 30px; /* Make space for the icon */
    }

    .search-icon {
      position: absolute;
      right: 5px;
      top: 50%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
      cursor: pointer;
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="search-container">
  <input type="text" class="search-input" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search...">

  <!-- SVG Icon (Reading Glass / Search Icon) -->
  <svg class="search-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
    <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"></circle>
    <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
  </svg>
</div>

<script>
  // Function to be called when the icon is clicked
  function handleSearch() {
    const query = document.getElementById('searchInput').value;
    alert('You searched for: ' + query);
    // You can replace the alert with your actual function logic
  }

  // Attach the click event to the SVG icon
  document.querySelector('.search-icon').addEventListener('click', handleSearch);
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

---

### 🔍 Explanation

- **`.search-container`**: A container to hold the input and the icon.
- **`.search-input`**: The input field with padding to make space for the icon.
- **`.search-icon`**: The SVG icon positioned absolutely to the right of the input.
- **`handleSearch()`**: A function that gets the input value and does something with it (like an alert or API call).
- **`addEventListener('click', handleSearch)`**: Makes the icon clickable and triggers the function.

---

